# Progress and commits

When a feature or phase is finished:

1. Check it off in `TRACKER.md` in the same change. Add a dated note only when the checkbox alone would hide a real decision.
2. Do not run `git init`, `git add`, `git commit`, or any command that writes git history.
3. Do not change git config. Do not pass `--author`. Do not add `Co-authored-by`, `Signed-off-by`, or any other author trailer. The commit Kaung runs uses his existing git identity.
4. If this folder is not a git repo yet, include `git init` in the command and still do not run it.
5. Show a PowerShell command he runs himself. The message says why the change exists, in one or two sentences. He may edit the message before running it.

```powershell
git add TRACKER.md <paths>
git commit -m @"
Why this change exists.

"@
```

```
Bad: the agent runs git commit, or adds Co-authored-by.
Good: TRACKER.md is checked off, then the command is shown and not executed.
```
